    {
      "claim": "Dihydroartemisinin, the structurally closest polycyclic lactone context, shows absolute oral bioavailability of 45% with 95% CI 34 to 56% in volunteers and 82% in healthy adults, supporting F at or above 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C17", "C23", "C28"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Digitoxin, a rigid polycyclic natural product, shows absolute oral bioavailability of about 90% in fasted healthy subjects, supporting high transferable exposure.",
      "card_ids": ["C19", "C32"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Lefamulin, a polycyclic diterpene, shows absolute oral bioavailability of 24 to 26% in fasted subjects, above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C06", "C38"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L1 context provides affirmative evidence of F below 20%; tacrolimus at about 20% is a lipophilic macrolide with poor structural transfer to this polar rigid lactone, and the single poor DHA report is contradicted by multiple measured DHA values of 45 to 85%.",
      "card_ids": ["C20", "C39"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "current_gold_voting_records",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "changed",
      "card_ids": ["C17", "C23", "C28", "C19", "C32", "C06", "C38"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental bioavailability data exist for the query molecule.",
    "No training context matches the query combination of high molecular weight, very low logD, and very high TPSA.",
    "The low prior rests on computational descriptors rather than measured permeability or absorption data.",
    "No context provides a measured F clearly below 20% that transfers to this polar rigid polycyclic lactone."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The physicochemical prior is low but uncertain and descriptor-based. L1 gold records across transferable contexts show absolute oral bioavailability at or above 20%, with the structurally closest context dihydroartemisinin at 45 to 85% and digitoxin at about 90%. No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F below 20%. Therefore F at or above 20% is better supported, giving a high prediction with moderate confidence."
}

